 <159788250+ClodoCapeo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:52:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(libobs): align current readback media time with audio

Agent-Role: eleven
Agent-Thread: 01a045e2-996f-7913-99f0-2cd237d3a6f8
Work-Unit: ZabLaboratory/Pulsar#253
Issue: #253
Evidence: native flash-click A/B measures picture advance without timestamp compensation
---
 libobs/obs-video.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libobs/obs-video.c b/libobs/obs-video.c
index 8b1542a23..835772524 100644
--- a/libobs/obs-video.c
+++ b/libobs/obs-video.c
@@ -974,6 +974,14 @@ static inline void output_frame(struct obs_core_video_mix *video)
 		deque_pop_front(&video->vframe_info_buffer, &vframe_info, sizeof(vframe_info));
 
 		frame.timestamp = vframe_info.timestamp;
+		/* A current CPU surface is one cadence interval newer than the
+		 * historical previous-surface readback. Advance its media clock by
+		 * that same interval, so removing the readback queue does not move
+		 * the picture ahead of the audio timeline. Preserve cadence/count
+		 * under renderer stalls; content identity remains independently exact.
+		 * The GPU-encoding path already uses its established timestamp map. */
+		if (current_readback && !gpu_active)
+			frame.timestamp += video_output_get_frame_time(video->video);
 		bool current_content = current_readback;
 #ifdef _WIN32
 		/* GPU encoding stages into the single copy_surfaces_encode set:
